  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Frequently people are building worlds and get errors in the build that prevent it from building successfully.  That's fine and debuggable, but the SDK will currently still try to launch/upload the world after a failure. \n\nThis manifests frequently as questions like: \n\"Why doesn't X change when I update my world?\"  or \"Why do I get kicked to the default world when I test build or join my uploaded world?\" \n\nIf it errored out before uploading if the build failed and gave a message to indicate that the user should check the console, that'd probably cut down on a lot of confusion for newer world creators. \n\n---\nVRC Build: 772 (n/a)\n\nPlatform: Windows (Unity)\n\nSDK: VRCSDK-2019.05.16.13.10  (and previous)",
